# Write clear summaries

<h2 id="add-something-the-title-does-not-say">Add something the title does not say</h2>

A summary is the line under a title: helper text on a card, a hint under a field or a notification preview. Do not repeat the title.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Living room lights. This card shows the living room lights. | Living room lights. 2 of 4 lights on. |
| Notification. You have a notification. | Front door. Opened at 22:15. |

<h2 id="use-common-words">Use clear and common words</h2>

Use the words people use for the thing, not the words on the device box.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Adjust the PIR trigger timeout. | Set how long the hallway light stays on after movement. |

<h2 id="keep-it-short">Keep it short</h2>

Put the main point first and aim for 160 characters or fewer. Cut anything the person does not need to decide.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| This schedule lets you decide, for every day of the week, the times at which the heating should switch on and off, and it can also be changed later. | Choose when the heating comes on and goes off each day. |

<h2 id="end-with-a-full-stop">End with a full stop</h2>

A full stop gives screen readers a clear pause.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Front door opened at 22:15 | Front door opened at 22:15. |

<h2 id="leave-out-introductory-words">Leave out introductory words</h2>

Do not say what type of thing it is.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Card: 6.2 kWh used so far today. | 6.2 kWh used so far today. |

<h2 id="start-with-a-verb">Start with a verb</h2>

Tell the person what they can do.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Heating times can be set here. | Set when the heating comes on. |

<h2 id="wg-053">Put help beside the decision</h2>

Place a hint where the person decides. Do not send them to another page to understand a field.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Duration (see the documentation for details) | Duration. How long the light stays on after movement, for example 5 minutes. |

<h2 id="wg-055">Support learning without overloading the task</h2>

Give the one fact needed now. Leave the detail for the full documentation.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Zigbee is a low-power mesh protocol that uses 2.4 GHz, supports hundreds of nodes and routes through mains-powered devices to extend range. | Mains-powered Zigbee devices pass messages along. Plug one in between the coordinator and the sensor. |

<h2 id="wg-056">Keep examples honest</h2>

Say it is an example and make sure it works in this home.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Entity ID: `light.reading_lamp` | Entity ID. For example, `light.reading_lamp`. Use the entity ID of your own light. |
